WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.630
so I hate to have to break it to you today
and just start the show on such a negative

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.950
note, especially to my progressive [inaudible]

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:10.530
audience members. But unless something changes
with a high likelihood, Donald Trump is very

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:15.840
rapidly barreling towards reelection in 2020
and this is why I've been very careful not

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.090
to make any statements when I report about,
Oh, you know, Georgia could conceivably be

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:25.579
in play, Texas could conceivably be in play.
Uh, there are a lot of uh, ifs, ands and buts

00:00:25.579 --> 00:00:30.640
attached to that and before we get into the
issues based components of my commentary today,

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.860
let's just deal with the math quickly because
there are people who are just putting way

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:39.410
too much confidence in the polling data that
shows Trump not doing well in North Carolina

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:44.390
and Georgia and Texas and Trump's approval
rating is tanking. And then there are also

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:50.150
people who just don't believe me when I say
that Donald Trump can get reelected even despite

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:55.420
a very low approval rating. The reality is
that what we saw in 2004 is the case.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.440
Anytime you're trying to unseat an incumbent
president, which is, it's really difficult.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:04.500
Donald Trump, uh, certainly very different
than George W. Bush in many ways, but as difficult

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:10.590
as it was to remove Bush in 2004, ultimately
not being removed. Of course, even someone

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:16.350
as malignantly ignorant and acutely narcissistic
as Donald Trump will be difficult to remove.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:20.740
Now from a mathematical perspective, when
half the country doesn't vote and you have

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:26.460
an electoral college system, that systemically
favors republicans in all of the ways that

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:33.399
we've talked about before, Donald Trump's
36 or 38 or 40% approval rating can easily

00:01:33.399 --> 00:01:39.369
get him re-elected. Now, I've said before,
you can construct the math such that it's

00:01:39.369 --> 00:01:44.600
possible to get reelected even with 27% approval,
and it's true. But if you disagree with me

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:48.670
about that or you think it's an exaggeration,
it's not even worth arguing about because

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:52.689
Trump's approval rating isn't that low and
there's no indication it's going to go that

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:53.689
low.

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:59.469
So with the math piece out of the way, let's
look at what Democrats are doing so far. Bearing

00:01:59.469 --> 00:02:05.469
in mind that we're still in the pre-primary
phase. Democrats need to run good campaigns

00:02:05.469 --> 00:02:10.640
with progressive ideas that are popular, of
course, but Democrats also need to at least

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:16.240
somewhat appeal to red state voters and moderates
in Purple States on the issues that clearly

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.740
matter right now. As I've said before, as
a strategy get out, the vote is much more

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:28.760
powerful than arguing with Trumpists, but
it still makes sense to at least stake out

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:35.210
positions, generally speaking, that will be
reasonable to some fraction of those moderate

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:40.500
Republican voters. There's unnecessary disclaimer
here. I'm being strategic here. I'm not talking

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:47.160
about what I like and what my politics are.
I'm talking about winning 2020 think about

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:54.110
immigration first. It's disgusting what's
happening at the border. It's a real humanitarian

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:59.290
crisis, but most of the conversations that
Democratic candidates are having are ridiculous

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:02.220
and debate moderators are hugely to blame
for this.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:07.180
As I've talked about before, what's happening
with the discussion around deportations on

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:12.730
the right is an absolute fantasy, right? I
mean, we're not going to deport 12 million

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:17.980
people who are in the United States illegally,
nor would we want to deport the 12 million

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:22.550
people that are in the United States illegally.
If people are committing violent crimes and

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:26.360
they're here illegally. Okay, they're, now
you're talking about people that it makes

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.110
sense to deport. But the reality is that there
are multiple industries that depend on these

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:36.031
undocumented immigrants, including agriculture,
including the restaurant industry. And they're

00:03:36.031 --> 00:03:42.540
a hugely positive influence on our society,
both economically and culturally from a a,

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:47.400
any number of standpoints from an American
dream standpoint, from a work ethic standpoint,

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.710
and basically every way that we can imagine.
Almost all of these undocumented immigrants

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:56.841
are actually a positive force here in the
United States. At the same time, democrats

00:03:56.841 --> 00:04:02.680
need to throw a bone to centrist and republican
voters around the need to have a defensible

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.730
border, a defended border.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:09.440
I've already debunked the idea of the wall
endless times and Democrats don't need to,

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:14.100
you know, pretend to be aggressive neo-cons
on the wall or even dabble with the xenophobic

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:19.320
or racist stuff, but something needs to be
done to just merely get on the record to Republican

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:24.040
voters that Democratic candidates understand
the concerns. There will be a defensible border

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:27.780
and no one is advocating for open borders
because they're going to try to smear all

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.200
the Democratic candidates as being in favor
of open borders when of course, that's not

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:37.040
the case. It should just be made clear that
no one is advocating for open borders because

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:42.470
that's the truth, but a little more is going
to need to be done and said if we don't want

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:48.160
to have the exact repetition of the 2016 election,
this isn't controversial, right? Every country

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:53.240
in the world that is an interesting and appealing
place for people to come to from other countries

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.520
is going to have a defended border.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:05:00.910
This wouldn't change under a Democratic president.
Let's just like go 5% further in making that

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:05.120
clear, but like I've said before, we end up
with all of this, you know, raise your hands

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:10.220
if you'd give undocumented immigrants healthcare,
even if that's a morally correct position

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:15.980
to take. It's a losing position if that becomes
the focus in the national election and Democrats

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:21.450
need to make damn sure that that doesn't actually
become the focus no matter what debate moderators

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:25.530
are going to try to do. Okay. Let's talk about
farmers and the Midwest, which we've been

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:29.680
talking about for months. At this point in
time. You have farmers in the Midwest who

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:35.020
are aware that it's Donald Trump's tariffs
that have been a disaster for them, but saying,

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:39.880
I will reverse the tariffs as many Democratic
candidates have been saying, is not going

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:44.220
to convince a lifelong Midwestern Republican
to vote for a Democrat.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:49.830
And I've said this before, when we hear about
all of these Trump voters in the Midwest who

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:54.380
are angry with Trump or disapprove of Trump,
or are farmers and recognize that Trump has

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:58.740
ruining their businesses, that doesn't mean
that you're going to go out and vote for a

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:05.300
Democrat in November of 2020 lifelong Republicans
who don't approve of Trump, aren't necessarily

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:10.990
voting for Joe Biden or Bernie Sanders or
Elizabeth Warren. So something more needs

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:16.860
to be done there. And it generally relates
to the economic anxieties of Middle America

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:22.139
that Hillary Clinton didn't do a good job
of addressing in an appropriate enough way.

00:06:22.139 --> 00:06:27.120
This is just the reality. I'm not saying the
narrative about disadvantaged white people

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:32.419
is based in any reality. It's ridiculous.
What I am saying is that without addressing

00:06:32.419 --> 00:06:38.930
some of these issues in a smart way, Trump
gets reelected period. This gets me to the

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:44.550
distraction attempts that have been very successful
by the right when Donald Trump generates a

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:51.280
firestorm around whether this or that person
is racist or whether a comment was racist

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:52.669
or whatever.

00:06:52.669 --> 00:06:58.830
These are important issues, but they are not
issues that are going to get swing state voters

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:04.699
to abandon Donald Trump or motivate anyone
to get out and vote. If they see an endless

00:07:04.699 --> 00:07:10.070
focus and debate over whether this or that
comment was racist as an example. Now I know

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:15.380
that there are people on the left who won't
like this, but it's just the reality and then

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:20.699
unfortunately I spoke a year ago about my
desire for this not to happen. Democrats and

00:07:20.699 --> 00:07:26.310
their supporters are starting to slam each
other in a way that could be self-destructive

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:31.560
and just help Donald Trump. We are seeing,
I'm going in no particular order here. We're

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:37.680
seeing a rise of a no Biden, no way contingent,
and I agree that Joe Biden is not a progressive,

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:43.020
but I also remember all those people who said
in 2016 who cares? Hillary would be the same

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:45.940
as Trump, and of course they couldn't have
been more wrong.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:52.190
Look at the Supreme Court. Look at the 25%
of a judges that Donald Trump has appointed

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:57.530
and we're reminded every day that and the
geopolitical belligerence and now trying to

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:02.180
collude with it, forcing collusion with another
country, Ukraine, we'll talk about that later,

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:05.900
could not have been more different from Hillary
Clinton, so that's a concern. Then we have

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:12.669
the growing group of Bernie supporters focusing
their ire on Elizabeth Warren, even mass unsubscribing

00:08:12.669 --> 00:08:18.030
from my youtube channel last week when I pointed
out, hey, in 60% of recent polls, Warren has

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:24.370
surpassed Bernie into second place. This group
claiming Warren is a tool of the establishment

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:29.889
to to appear progressive and I'm a shill merely
for mentioning poll results. Bernie and Warren

00:08:29.889 --> 00:08:36.529
are not the same. That's clear, but that is
another contingent that is potentially self-destructive

00:08:36.529 --> 00:08:40.270
and it's getting to the point where it could
be damaging. In the general election, the

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:45.050
Tulsi people, I've already talked about, Andrew
Yang's followers, who although relatively

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:49.760
small mathematically are getting extremely
angry with just like everything, every, anything

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:52.149
that happens there absolutely furious about.

00:08:52.149 --> 00:08:58.930
Then you've got Biden supporters who are falling
for the often repeated right wing talking

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:05.601
points about Bernie and Warren are extreme.
They are radical. They're too far left. They're

00:09:05.601 --> 00:09:10.790
even talking about the term socialism that's
there. There's a contingent of Biden's supporters.

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:16.450
That's terrible. This is the type of stuff
that will propel Donald Trump to reelection

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:23.480
because it feeds narratives that are not useful
to the left, so I'm not saying this because

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:29.180
I'm looking to attack a particular candidate
or the supporters of a particular candidate.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:36.320
This isn't even about particular candidates.
This is merely pragmatism. We saw what happened

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:42.190
in 2016 and unless we prevent these things
I'm mentioning from getting completely out

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:46.120
of control, it's going to happen again and
we'll have four more years of Trump. Now,

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:51.610
there are people in the audience who would
rather have four more years of Trump. Then

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:54.180
whoever you don't like from the Democratic
primary, right?

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:59.080
There are people who would say, burn it all
down, let Trump do whatever he wants to do

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:04.350
because it's better than having whoever it
is that's running in the Democratic primary.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:09.860
I just disagree with that as a strategy. I
think that the more we look at history, the

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:17.950
more we realize that what has worked historically
is not uh, foregoing small changes we could

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:23.240
make right now with the idea of eventually
burning it all down and building it back up

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:27.980
in a perfect image of what is perfectly aligned
with our political ideology. That's not the

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:33.330
way it's worked in the last however many,
however, however many years you consider to

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:38.990
be modern politics. That's simply not a strategy
that's worked. So I'm open to having my mind

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:43.591
change. If you think you can convince me that
the let Trump have another four years, burn

00:10:43.591 --> 00:10:47.890
it all down and then we'll be in a much better
position for 2020 for mentality. If you want

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:51.940
to try to convince me of that, I'm more than
open to hearing from you, but it's not something

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:56.209
that I see backed by history. It's not something
I see backed by logic and it's not something

00:10:56.209 --> 00:10:59.870
that seems like the right approach. Let me
know what you think. I'm open to having my

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:05.550
mind changed about all of this, but I am increasingly
concerned because I don't want to see another

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:09.750
four years of Donald Trump. Yeah, I know it'd
be great for the show, but I care about the

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.720
country even more than that.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:15.140
Uh, and I want to hear it from you. If you
disagree with me, I'm on Twitter at d pacman.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:15.191
The show is on Twitter at David Pakman show

